dexed":false,"ogImage":"/uploads/blog/fd-calculator-calculate-fixed-deposit-returns-easily.webp","twitterImage":"/uploads/blog/fd-calculator-calculate-fixed-deposit-returns-easily.webp","faqJson":[{"answer":"An FD Calculator is an online tool that estimates the maturity amount and interest earned on a Fixed Deposit based on your investment amount, interest rate, tenure, and compounding frequency.","question":"What is an FD Calculator?"},{"answer":"FD interest is calculated using either simple interest or compound interest, depending on the financial institution and the type of Fixed Deposit.","question":"How is FD interest calculated?"},{"answer":"You'll typically need your investment amount, annual interest rate, deposit tenure, and compounding frequency to estimate your returns.","question":"What information do I need to use an FD Calculator?"},{"answer":"Many banks allow premature withdrawal, but penalties or reduced interest rates may apply. Check your bank's specific terms before investing.","question":"Can I withdraw my Fixed Deposit before maturity?"}],"toc":[{"id":"heading-0","text":"1. Principal Amount","level":2},{"id":"heading-1","text":"2. Interest Rate","level":2},{"id":"heading-2","text":"3. Deposit Tenure","level":2},{"id":"heading-3","text":"4. Compounding Frequency","level":2},{"id":"heading-4","text":"Investment Amount","level":2},{"id":"heading-5","text":"Interest Rate","level":2},{"id":"heading-6","text":"Investment Duration","level":2},{"id":"heading-7","text":"Compounding Frequency","level":2},{"id":"heading-8","text":"Type of Fixed Deposit","level":2},{"id":"heading-9","text":"Regular Fixed Deposit","level":2},{"id":"heading-10","text":"Tax-Saving Fixed Deposit","level":2},{"id":"heading-11","text":"Senior Citizen Fixed Deposit","level":2},{"id":"heading-12","text":"Cumulative Fixed Deposit","level":2},{"id":"heading-13","text":"Non-Cumulative Fixed Deposit","level":2},{"id":"heading-14","text":"Saves Time","level":3},{"id":"heading-15","text"